# Local docs
docs/local/

# Everything a fuzzing campaign writes: the working corpus it grows, the crashing inputs
# it drops, the coverage profiles. Named here because a fuzzer is the one tool in this
# tree that creates files nobody asked for - it copies its seeds, mutates them, and writes
# a new file for every input it minimises. fuzz/seeds/ and fuzz/regressions/ are NOT
# ignored: the seeds are generated by fuzz/make-seeds.py and reviewed, and a regression is
# a crashing input somebody chose to commit.
/fuzz/work/
